st0:"Opening",st0d:"Six reasons to stock up with a local supplier.",st1:"Logistics",st1d:"Order today, receive tomorrow.",st2:"Close support",st2d:"Real people on the other side.",st3:"Our culture",st3d:"Respect, listening and dialogue.",st4:"Suppliers",st4d:"Selected brands and partners.",st5:"No red tape",st5d:"Ordered, paid, delivered.",st6:"Businesses only",st6d:"Who can buy, said up front.",st7:"Lead times",st7d:"Days, hours and shipping in blocks.",
st0_alt:"Series opening: Why GP?",st1_alt:"Logistics story.",st2_alt:"Close support story.",st3_alt:"Our culture story.",st4_alt:"Trusted suppliers story.",st5_alt:"No red tape story.",st6_alt:"Business-only sales story.",st7_alt:"Order today, receive by tomorrow story.",
car_t:"The carousel, unfolded",car_d:"The same series in the feed. Each slide has a number, a short title and a visual detail that leads to the next: the road continues from one image to the other.",car_c:"Slides 1 and 2 of the “Why GP?” carousel, side by side as they appear when swiping.",car1_alt:"Slide 1: Respect, listening and dialogue.",car2_alt:"Slide 2: Bought today, arrives tomorrow.",
a4c:"Standardized cards",a4cp:"One pattern per segment and per holiday: the same colors, the same notice bar, the same place for the price.",
sy0:"Modernized logo.",sy0o:"Old logo.",logo_old_alt:"Old GP Atacado logo, white on blue, with the GP letters, the word ATACADO and a truck.",k_tools_v:"Figma, Google Forms, Slack and Notion",sy1:"Offer of the day.",sy2:"Holiday: Black Friday.",sy3:"Price list of the day, by segment.",logo_alt:"Modernized GP Atacado logo in white on blue.",sy1_alt:"Offer of the day card.",sy2_alt:"Black Friday card.",sy3_alt:"Price list of the day card for beers.",
a5:"Internal tools",a5_lead:"Controls that used to be done by hand became simple tools, each with an owner. All built with Claude.",a5_note:"Employee and client names and real financial figures are hidden.",
t1:"Time sheet",t1p:"Hours written down by hand and added up at the end of the month.",t1s:"Clock-in, lunch and clock-out per employee, in each person’s pay cycle, with hour balance and CSV export.",t1_alt:"Time sheet screen: standard workday, pay cycle and backup.",
t4:"Cargo in and out control",t4p:"Cargo in and out tracked by hand, with no single place to check.",t4s:"An overview of what is waiting to leave, on the road, delivered or with a problem.",t4_alt:"Dispatch control panel: orders waiting, on the road and delivered.",
t2:"Financial dashboard",t2p:"The owner had no simple view of the month’s numbers.",t2s:"One screen per month with gross revenue, net and entries, plus a backup reminder.",t2w:"Built for the owner. Values hidden in this image.",t2_alt:"Financial dashboard with blurred values.",
t3:"Service priority matrix",t3p:"Services with no clear priority order or defined owner.",t3s:"Each service rated by impact and urgency, with status, deadline and owner, seen in real time by the people who decide.",t3_alt:"Service matrix split into Plan and Do now.",
t5:"Billing and order summary",t5p:"Each billing message was put together by hand, one by one.",t5s:"The order generates the billing message with a summary, ready to send on WhatsApp.",t5_alt:"Billing screen: client details and a preview of the order message.",
a6:"Result",a6p:"increase in sales, comparing 2026 with 2025.",a6l1:"Community clients started buying more through direct contact.",a6l2:"Automated processes, with each employee owning their part.",a6l3:"Continuous improvement: the work is ongoing.",
a7:"Learning",a7q:"Design happens where the problem is: at the counter, on the truck, on WhatsApp.",a7p:"I learned to measure change by client behavior and the team’s routine, not by aesthetics.",
